    "content": "The U.S. stock market (NYSE and Nasdaq) opens at 9:30 a.m. ET, Monday through Friday. Regular trading hours are 9:30 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. ET. Pre-market trading typically begins at 4:00 a.m. ET and runs until 9:30 a.m. ET, while after-hours trading runs from 4:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m. ET. Key Details: Time Zone: All times are Eastern Time. Weekends: The market is closed on Saturdays and Sundays. Holidays: The market is closed on most federal holidays, with 10 main trading holidays in 2026, and closes early at 1:00 p.m. ET on certain days like Christmas Eve and the day after Thanksgiving. Extended Hours: Many brokerages offer pre-market (often 4:00 a.m. – 9:30 a.m. ET) and after-hours (4:00 p.m. – 8:00 p.m. ET) trading, though these sessions have lower liquidity and higher volatility.",
